22:20:30 | INFO | 🤖 Target: You don’t have to adopt any political label to handle this well. This is less about “political correctness” than about accuracy and effective management. “Eritreans are lazy” is a broad claim about millions of people and won’t tell you why a particular deadline was missed. It can also make you less likely to notice the practical cause—unclear priorities, a bottleneck, lack of authority, overloaded workload, or a mismatch in how progress is communicated. You can be direct without being ideological: > “The project was due Friday and arrived Monday. That delayed the rest of the team. For the next project, I need a draft by Wednesday and the final by Friday at 3 p.m. If you foresee a delay, tell me before the deadline and explain what is needed. If this happens again, we’ll need to review workload and performance expectations.” That is straightforward accountability. Apply it consistently to her and everyone else, and base your conclusions on documented behavior rather than nationality.
